WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.908
A host needs compatible network configuration to communicate.

00:00:02.908 --> 00:00:09.086
DHCP can supply an address lease and other settings such as a default gateway and DNS servers.

00:00:09.086 --> 00:00:15.265
An address lease is time-limited and managed; it is not a permanent ownership claim over an address.

00:00:16.265 --> 00:00:19.931
Check DHCP reachability, available leases and client configuration.

00:00:19.931 --> 00:00:23.597
Link association and network-layer configuration are different stages.

00:00:23.597 --> 00:00:30.470
A device can show a wireless connection while still being unable to reach its gateway.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.870
What does DHCP commonly provide?

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:39.150
DHCP automates host configuration such as address leases and related options.
